 "mapping": {
  "author": "claude-mapper-m20-2",
  "date": "2026-11-05",
  "draft_py": "# Yarok's Fenlurker: \"When this creature enters, each opponent exiles a card from their hand.\"\n# Goremand / Ruin Crab's EachPlayer(ALL_OPPONENTS, ...) with the inner effect YOU-relative (the\n# rotated opponent). The inner atom is the compiler's hand-move lane (Liliana's Steward's discard\n# shape: cards CHOOSE 1 from hand, controller = the chooser, from = HAND), with the exile\n# destination Zone(EXILE, OWNER) of every compiled \"exile\" (not a discard: no journal_kind).\netb = TriggeredAbility(\n    event=ZoneChangeEvent(\n        from_zone=Zone(kind=ZoneKind.ANY, controller=ControllerRef.ANY),\n        to_zone=Zone(kind=ZoneKind.BATTLEFIELD, controller=ControllerRef.YOU),\n        subject=FAtom(pred=FAtomPred.IS_SOURCE),\n    ),\n    condition=None,\n    effect=EachPlayer(\n        ref=ControllerRef.ALL_OPPONENTS,\n        effect=A(Verb.MOVE_ZONE, {\n            'cards': Selector(\n                count=QConst(value=1),\n                mode=SelectorMode.CHOOSE,\n                filter=FAnd(children=()),\n                zones=(Zone(kind=ZoneKind.HAND, controller=ControllerRef.YOU),),\n            ),\n            'controller': ControllerRef.YOU,\n            'destination': Zone(kind=ZoneKind.EXILE, controller=ControllerRef.OWNER),\n            'from': Zone(kind=ZoneKind.HAND, controller=ControllerRef.YOU),\n        }),\n    ),\n)\nabilities = [etb, *compiled]\n",
  "clauses": [
   {
    "clause": "When this creature enters, each opponent exiles a card from their hand.",
    "ir": "abilities[0]"
   },
   {
    "clause": "{2}{B}: This creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.",
    "ir": "abilities[1]"
   }
  ],
  "g0_warnings": [],
  "notes": "The canonicalizer promotes the hand pick to ONE_OF (the compiler exempts Goremand / Liliana's Steward by name, PICK_ASK_FORCE_SILENT L-27). Inside EachPlayer the ONE_OF ask's deciding seat (asking_seat) is the rotated opponent, so the opponent chooses; the one_of tag carries no seat, and collectors that credit asks to the active player (B-53 open item) would let the caster choose."
 },
